Z||000013||RiceCooker||04-23-2001||07:45 PM||||I would like to express my elation for my team in the draft.<P>I think we might have given up too much, (#21 + second rounder) but we got maybe the best OT in the draft - Kenyatta Walker.<P>Do you honestly think, Leonard Davis would have been rated #1 if he was 50 lbs lighter? Nope. Teams were just drooling over his size.<BR>Go Bucs!<P>Aother great first day went to da bears getting a couple of wolverines.<P>They missed out on their man Andre Carter DE because of the 49ers, but they had to grab Terrell beacuse he was arguably the best athlete in the draft. Another super picjup in RB Anthony Thomas.<BR>If Cade McNown can't do it this year for the bears, he will be labelled a bust and be shipped right outta town. He's got the kind of weapons young QB's dream about.<P>Same goes for Akili smith. WR's Peter Warrick Chad Johnson (oregon state) Darnay scott, HB Corey Dillon. Smith better produce.<P>more to come....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Kids in the back seat cause accidents<BR>Accidents in the back seat cause kids||||reg||1
Z||000014||BENGAL4||04-23-2001||09:58 PM||||Another confusing draft day in Cincinnati. I am happy, however,  with Justin Smith. This guy is a throwback to hard work and determination. His motor runs for 60 minutes just like Takeo Spikes. We could use 40 more of that type on the team. As for the rest of the draft, Chad Johnson was an OK pick. With Darnay Scott questionable, we needed another deep threat. But the rest of the picks, I wonder what the brain trust is thinking about. Sean Brewer? Who the hell is that? The fastest TE in the draft? Big deal. We need to fill alot of holes, but wasting a 3rd round pick on a guy that they probably could have gotten in the fifth, sixth or seventh round. ???????<P>Ricecooker, Kenyatta Walker is not the best OT in the draft, but he should turn out to be a decent pick for the Bucs. As big as Leonard Davis is, 370 lbs, he has only 18% body fat. Davis gave up 1 sack last year and that was to Justin Smith. I also agree with you that Akili Smith is on borrowed time. If we could have signed Grbac, Akili could have stayed at home in San Diego. <P>April, my favorite time of year because we are equal with every other team until mid September.<P>     ||||reg||5
